+   once, on the group, and nothing else declares that an option is a tile. Every
+   group, and every SegmentedTabs strip, resets it to `none`, so a value on an
+   ancestor of a group never reaches the group's options, and a strip's tabs are
+   always pills. An option and everything inside it inherit the value above the
+   option and cannot write their own (the pin in toggle-group/styles.css), so each
+   option has one value, and every reader reads that one: the pill's one-row law
+   below and in toggle-group/styles.css, the tile's plate (`flush` paints no plate at
+   rest, Q-2 (b); `plated` keeps the control plate), the selected perimeter, and the
